A||N||12||mblackwell||Adding remote decklid release||||1||
Z||000000||mblackwell||06-15-2001||11:24 PM||||The previous owner of my Fiero had an Ungo 6200 alarm system installed in 1994.  All it is set up to do is keyless entry, ignition disable, and the alarm sounds if a door is opened.  No motion or impact detection, even though the alarm supports it. I don't care about not having that stuff though, it would probably just annoy innocent bystanders anyway.<P>The remote has two buttons, the second button doesn't do anything.  How hard would it be to make it the decklid release botton?  I only want to do this because it would be cool, if it is difficult I probably wont bother trying it.<P>In the manual one of the wires is labeld "botton 2 feature, to external relay."<BR>So, would this work?<P>1. Locate brain (I have no diea where it is, any ideas?)<BR>2. Locate decklid release relay.<BR>3. Run a wire from the secondaey feature thing on the brain to the decklid release relay.<P>Is that all there is to it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||06-15-2001||11:55 PM||||power trunk relay is located in center of dash next to heater control head.  To operate you have to feed power to black/white wire.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mblackwell||06-16-2001||12:03 AM||||Can you get to the relay by removing the bezel and radio?  What about tapping the wire in an easier to reach location?  <P>Also, was the power trunk available on the formula?  If not, mine was added later and the thing could be anywhere.||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-16-2001||12:08 AM||||Yes you could splice in any where really.  I would think that a formula would come with power trunk.<BR>Its location is near the heater control head, may be easily accessible from under dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mblackwell||06-16-2001||12:14 AM||||Thanks!<P>Now I just hafta find the alarm brain.<BR>What size are the torx screws that are all over the interior?||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||06-16-2001||12:37 AM||||t15||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadaver||06-16-2001||01:18 PM||||No the trunk relay is located just right of the steering column under the dash. <BR>When I hooked up my trunk I just ran the wire to the back side of the switch in the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||06-16-2001||02:47 PM||||Iv taken my dash out 4 times and don't ever remeber seeing the trunk relay there, but it could be. I would find it easier to just tap into the wire right behind the switch, on the right of the guage cluster. <P>As far as where the brain is located, that could be a jod finding. I would just find a wire, like the trigger for the doors (probally tapped right behind the little button that turns on the entry lights) and follow it back to the brain. It is probally mounted under the dash somewhere. I would start looking over by the blue dingy thingy and that area, as it is the easiest to reach. Sometimes they mount them behind the kickpanels, but I don't believe the fiero's are large enough to fit a normal sized brain box in. One other easy wire to follow would be the annennta, if your alarm system has one. Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000008||mblackwell||06-16-2001||07:20 PM||||I still can't find the brain.  I looked behind the radio, under the dash, behind the carpet, and under the seats.<P>When I activate the alarm I hear a clicking sound,  From the ECM enclosure.  The overide switch wires also seem to go into the ECM.  Is there room in there for it?  Is that part of the console easy to remove?||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||06-17-2001||03:06 AM||||Hmmm it might be behind the ecm cover?<BR>You need to remove the shifter knob and the surround then remove the rear part of the console||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tina||06-17-2001||10:57 AM||||If I remember right, it was on the on the left side underneath the shift console and <BR>radio/heater control.<BR>Underneath the plastic sceleton.<BR>Almost underneath the dash but not quit.<P>Hope it helps.<BR>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||prtzlboy||06-17-2001||10:46 PM||||Ok, I'm not trying to insult anyone's intelligence here, but did you try pressing and *holding* the second button on the remote?  I have seen people buy cars with aftermarket keyless entry and trunk go for weeks without figuring this out.  I'm just trying to maybe save you some headaches *just in case* you haven't done this.||||reg||12
